<title>JORDAN: Jordan ministry gets loan for grain purchases.</title>
<headline>Jordan ministry gets loan for grain purchases.</headline>
<dateline>AMMAN 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jordan's Ministry of Supply signed a 25 million dinar loan on Tuesday with Jordan Islamic Bank to help finance its grains purchases, officials said.</p>
<p>Supply ministry officials said the loan will help finance stepped-up wheat purchases to honour a government pledge to decrease fixed bread prices once cheaper wheat is available.</p>
<p>The loan will include financing a large purchase last month of 150,000 tonnes of Argentine, Australian and Canadian hard red winter wheat at $164.94 per tonne in three equal lots, for delivery in November, December and January.</p>
<p>The loan will be paid in six instalments with four months grace period. No other details were immediately available.</p>
<p>Jordan Islamic Bank has provided the Ministry of Supply with over 250 million dinars in financing for rice, sugar and animal feed imports over the last three years, bank officials said.</p>
<p>($1 = 0.7080 dinar)</p>
<p>-- Amman Newsroom 9626-623776</p>
